<section class="section" id="source-timeline" aria-labelledby="timeline-heading">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">Dated Source Trail</p>
    <h2 id="timeline-heading">Notification and planning timeline</h2>
  </div>

  <div class="info-grid">
    <article class="info-card">
      <span class="route-kicker">9 April 2013</span>
      <h3>Tiger reserve notified</h3>
      <p>
        Notification F.3(8)Forest/2012 declared 41,717.188 hectares as Critical Tiger Habitat and
        34,282.274 hectares as buffer, totalling 75,999.462 hectares. The Rajasthan Gazette copy was
        published on 18 April 2013.
      </p>
      <a href="https://forest.rajasthan.gov.in/content/dam/raj/forest/ForestDepartment/PDFs/Department%20Wing/Wildlife/Protectedarea/MHTR%20-ESZ%20Notification%209%20April%202013.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open the 2013 Gazette scan</a>
    </article>

    <article class="info-card">
      <span class="route-kicker">25 November 2020</span>
      <h3>Final ESZ notified</h3>
      <p>
        MoEFCC notification S.O. 4268(E) established a 248.70 sq km Eco-Sensitive Zone, varying from
        zero to one kilometre. The final notification is dated 25 November and the Gazette issue is dated
        27 November; 10 January 2020 was the earlier draft-notification date.
      </p>
      <a href="https://moef.gov.in/uploads/2020/12/mukundra-1.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open the final ESZ Gazette</a>
    </article>

    <article class="info-card">
      <span class="route-kicker">24 April 2023</span>
      <h3>Expansion received in-principle approval</h3>
      <p>
        The Rajasthan LTAP records NTCA technical in-principle approval for a proposed MHTR expansion.
        The document expressly makes subsequent notification conditional on consent and State approval.
      </p>
      <a href="https://forest.rajasthan.gov.in/content/dam/raj/forest/ForestDepartment/PDFs/Department%20Wing/Wildlife/Long%20term%20action%20plan%20Final%20Updated%20maps.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open the Long Term Action Plan</a>
    </article>

    <article class="info-card">
      <span class="route-kicker">5 October 2023</span>
      <h3>Core and buffer schedules amended</h3>
      <p>
        Notification F.3(22)Forest/2023 revised the legal total to 1,135.787 sq km and inserted
        Bhainsrodgarh-area entries into the Critical Tiger Habitat schedule.
      </p>
      <a href="https://forest.rajasthan.gov.in/content/dam/raj/forest/ForestDepartment/PDFs/Department%20Wing/Wildlife/Protectedarea/Mukundra%20hills_0001_1.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open the 2023 notification</a>
    </article>

    <article class="info-card">
      <span class="route-kicker">7 December 2023</span>
      <h3>ESZ Zonal Master Plan published</h3>
      <p>
        The plan organises the ESZ regulatory framework, land-use context and development controls.
        It implements the ESZ planning requirement; it does not replace the tiger-reserve notification.
      </p>
      <a href="https://forest.rajasthan.gov.in/content/dam/raj/forest/ForestDepartment/PDFs/Department%20Wing/Wildlife/Sanction-Zonal-Master-Plan/ZMP_MHTR071223.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open the Zonal Master Plan</a>
    </article>

    <article class="info-card">
      <span class="route-kicker">1 June 2026</span>
      <h3>Department ESZ KML updated</h3>
      <p>
        The Forest Department download register lists the MHTR reserve KML as dated 31 July 2018 and
        a separate ESZ KML as updated on 1 June 2026. The two files therefore have different subjects
        and update dates.
      </p>
      <a href="https://forest.rajasthan.gov.in/content/raj/forest/en/aboutus/departmental-wings/forest-devlopment/districtwise-forest-blocks-google-earth.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open the official KML register</a>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section split-panel" aria-labelledby="esz-heading">
  <div>
    <p class="eyebrow">Eco-Sensitive Zone</p>
    <h2 id="esz-heading">The ESZ is a variable-width regulatory zone</h2>
    <p>
      The final Gazette describes an ESZ extending from zero to one kilometre around the reserve and
      covering 248.70 sq km. Zero extent occurs in directions where the notification records
      co-termination with the tiger-reserve buffer. The Gazette also provides boundary descriptions,
      coordinates, maps and a village list.
    </p>
    <p>
      The ESZ does not prohibit every activity. The notification and Zonal Master Plan distinguish
      prohibited, regulated and promoted activities. Site-specific permissions remain the responsibility
      of the competent government authorities.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="scope-list" aria-label="ESZ interpretation">
    <div><strong>248.70 sq km</strong><span>Notified ESZ area.</span></div>
    <div><strong>0–1 km</strong><span>Variable outward extent stated in the Gazette.</span></div>
    <div><strong>75 villages</strong><span>Count recorded in the 2023 Zonal Master Plan.</span></div>
    <div><strong>Separate legal layer</strong><span>Not part of the core-plus-buffer total.</span></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="kml-heading">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">GIS Interpretation</p>
    <h2 id="kml-heading">How the 2026 ESZ KML should be used</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="grid-2">
    <article class="card">
      <h3>Appropriate use</h3>
      <ul class="check-list">
        <li>Show a dated ESZ outer-limit or context overlay.</li>
        <li>Retain the source label “Rajasthan Forest Department, ESZ KML as on 01.06.2026”.</li>
        <li>Read the geometry with the 2020 Gazette and 2023 Zonal Master Plan.</li>
        <li>Use the notification schedules and revenue records for legal interpretation.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <h3>Incorrect use</h3>
      <ul class="check-list">
        <li>Do not replace the reserve or Critical Tiger Habitat polygon with the ESZ KML.</li>
        <li>Do not colour the complete enclosed footprint as 248.70 sq km of ESZ.</li>
        <li>Do not describe a KML calculation as a notified legal area.</li>
        <li>Do not infer the meaning of unlabelled internal geometry without an official legend.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

